# GATBOX disk imaging (installed by gatbox-bootstrap.sh; docs/plans/2026-11-02-disk-imaging.md §5).
#
# A whole disk behind a USB bridge (the dock, a card reader, the image store's own case): group gatbox-disk, which only
# the disk job's user holds, may read and write it, and the desktop is told to leave it alone (no auto-mount, no
# file-manager entry). The image store is mounted by its own unit (srv-gatbox-disks.mount), which this does not affect.
#
# SUBSYSTEMS (plural) matches any parent in the usb subsystem. ENV{ID_BUS}=="usb" would not do: once udev has asked a SATA
# drive through the dock, ID_BUS is "ata" (Task 0, 2026-11-06), so that match would miss exactly the drives this is for.
# mmcblk and nvme are not behind USB, so they stay root:disk, and so do partitions (DEVTYPE "partition").
SUBSYSTEM=="block", ENV{DEVTYPE}=="disk", SUBSYSTEMS=="usb", GROUP="gatbox-disk", MODE="0660", ENV{UDISKS_IGNORE}="1"
#
# udisks reads UDISKS_IGNORE from each block device, not from the disk it sits on: with the line above alone, the desktop
# mounted a CF card's FAT partition read-write as it appeared (the Pi, 2026-11-15), and a read-write FAT mount sets the dirty
# flag in the card's boot sector. So a partition behind USB is ignored too. It keeps its group and mode (root:disk): only the
# flag is set. The bootstrap's re-trigger reaches whole disks only, so a card already in the dock when the rule is installed
# is ignored from its next plug-in.
SUBSYSTEM=="block", ENV{DEVTYPE}=="partition", SUBSYSTEMS=="usb", ENV{UDISKS_IGNORE}="1"
